State in Compose is any value that changes over time and drives the UI. A state held in a composable is remembered across recompositions with remember. A plain val resets every recomposition.

```kotlin
@Composable
fun Counter() {
    var count by remember { mutableStateOf(0) }
    Button(onClick = { count++ }) { Text("$count") }
}
```

This works because Compose keeps the remembered slot for the count and re-reads it on every recomposition, redrawing only the Text that reads the state.
